package parser

import "strings"

// oracleParameters holds every name the pinned Oracle (testdata/pins.tsv)
// answers for an initialization parameter: the 566 V$PARAMETER lists in
// FREEPDB1, read on 2026-11-19 with
//
//	SELECT name FROM v$parameter ORDER BY name
//
// and the 7,137 hidden names X$KSPPI lists there, 7,134 of them absent from
// V$PARAMETER, read as SYS with
//
//	ALTER SESSION SET CONTAINER = FREEPDB1;
//	SELECT ksppinm FROM x$ksppi WHERE ksppinm LIKE '\_%' ESCAPE '\' ORDER BY 1
//
// X$KSPPI is the server's own parameter table; a hidden parameter is not in
// V$PARAMETER until it is set, and Oracle accepts these names too
// ("_ORACLE_SCRIPT" among them, which DROP-PLUGGABLE-DATABASE.txt writes).
// ALTER SESSION SET and ALTER SYSTEM SET look a name up while they parse and
// answer ORA-02248 or ORA-02065 at a name neither list holds, so the name is
// refused before the '=' or the value after it is read. The list is not a
// list of parameters a session may change: Oracle's parse accepts a parameter
// it cannot modify and answers ORA-02095 or ORA-02096 at the name, which is
// still a rejection at the same byte. Names are case-insensitive.
//
// Ref: ALTER-SESSION.bnf and ALTER-SYSTEM.bnf, alter_session_set_clause and
// alter_system_set_clause; the server's lists are V$PARAMETER and X$KSPPI.
